shoot:description:I went back to the coast, again looking for Elegant Tern, and found a couple this time!  They flew in circles in the area for a minute, and they were kind of loud in announcing their presence.  I also got another lifer: Baird's Sandpiper.  This sandpiper was kind of by itself, not hanging out with the small flock of Western and Least Sandpipers that were also there.  I noticed the extra-long wings, and knew what it was.  Finally!  I've not had luck in looking for these birds the last few years.  Aside from those birds, I also spent a few minutes laying down in some dry sand, and the sandpiper flock eventually came close.  A juvenile Semipalmated Plover was the most curious of the bunch.  The photos didn't come out super sharp but it was fun to spend a few minutes at eye level with these birds.
